{"nodes": [{"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1411", "label": "Register 1411 \u2014 what is untested, stated plainly", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The trajectory re-places a at six block openings but only lanthanum is a recorded value, so agreement at the other five is untested rather than confirmed; the rule and the endpoint rule of 1403 differ in precision and recall and are not yet distinguishable from the record."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1412", "label": "Register 1412 \u2014 the law has no residue; the trajectory does", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two assertions had been conflated: the least-nu law (tested by corridor non-emptiness, 106 of 106) and the trajectory (a particular sequence of a values). Every failure of the preceding twenty exchanges lives in the second, not the first."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1413", "label": "Register 1413 \u2014 ninety-nine of one hundred and six, nothing fitted", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The seven remaining misses (Mn 25, Tc 43, Ce 58, Gd 64, Pa 91, Cm 96, Rf 104) are identical under both placement rules, so they are placement-independent and every one is an aufbau exception."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1414", "label": "Register 1414 \u2014 the floor exists exactly when the entrant has nodes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A read parity object was the placement rule's own output; measured from the corridors instead, the floor is minus infinity exactly when n \u2212 l \u2212 1 = 0, derivable rather than observed. Reading a pattern in one's own output was the fault that recurred all day."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1415", "label": "Register 1415 \u2014 the two bounds come from different blocks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ceiling binds within the entrant's own Janet block 85% of the time; floor binds in the next block 89%. Both exception sets are homogeneous and named: eleven ceiling exceptions all s-against-s, six floor exceptions all f or d intruders."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1416", "label": "Register 1416 \u2014 delta equals a times root p fails", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The failure is the identification, not register 1341: 1341 says a and delta share an index, not that one number equals the other. The likely cause is that measured delta is the Rydberg channel's while the walk's a governs the last bound electron \u2014 different electrons, different regimes."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1417", "label": "Register 1417 \u2014 Lambda_traj, the trajectory as an index", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every closing axis is a property the electron has before it moves; every axis describing where it lands fails. Later corrected by 1418 as overstated."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1418", "label": "Register 1418 \u2014 Lambda_traj is a projection of Lambda, not a new index", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replacing n by n \u2212 l \u2212 1 is a relabelling that changes nothing \u2014 A.erel exactly. Before calling a coordinate system new, ask whether its axes are the parent's letters relabelled."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1419", "label": "Register 1419 \u2014 the adjunction test confirms A.derived directly", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replace is re-coordinatisation and is free (E stays 0, box 48 to 56); adjoin is adjunction and is forbidden (E 0 to 47, box 24 to 168). The two operations are now separated by measurement rather than argument."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1420", "label": "Register 1420 \u2014 the landing axes refuse at q equal to two", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "q = 2 is the twelve donor steps. Lambda's cell is a transition with a source triple and a target triple; the walk's cell carried only the target, and the bracket construction never records the source."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_corridor_test", "label": "The corridor test as falsifier", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It works in both directions: the nuclear shell model's six pairs give an empty feasible set and the form is refuted; the atomic corridor is non-empty at every element and the form survives. That asymmetry is the corridor doing the job it was built for."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_nu_law", "label": "The least-nu law (Pauli-admissible subshell of least nu)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A law cannot have residue and this one does not: 106 of 106 corridors are non-empty. The caveat kept is gadolinium and curium, where the corridor is non-empty but its midpoint selects the rival."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_handshake_placement", "label": "The handshake placement of a, against per-block ascent", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Handshake gives 99/106 with ten moves against per-block ascent's 97 with fifteen \u2014 better on both counts. Per-block ascent never violates a corridor but re-places a where nothing requires it."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_madelung_tiebreak", "label": "Madelung preference as the resolution of an exact degeneracy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At a = L entrant and rival are exactly degenerate (potassium 19: both 4s and 3d score 3.000000). Breaking toward the higher n gives 97/106 against 91 for the lower \u2014 the Madelung preference appearing as a tie-break rather than an imposed rule."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_lambda_traj", "label": "Lambda_traj", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_a_derived", "label": "A.derived \u2014 adjoining a derived coordinate cannot repair closure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The box grows by the derived coordinate's value count while the cell count is fixed, so adjunction does not merely fail to help \u2014 it destroys closure."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_a_erel", "label": "A.erel \u2014 E is relative to a coordinatisation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A lattice property belongs to the coordinatisation and not to the underlying set, so a relabelling that preserves information may move the box without moving E."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_aufbau_exception_set", "label": "The seven placement-independent aufbau exceptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_quantum_defect_channel", "label": "Quantum defect delta and the Rydberg channel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1412", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_nu_law", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1412", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_corridor_test", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_corridor_test", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_nu_law", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1411-1420.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_register_1411", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1411_1420_handshake_placement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/